4. RESTRICTIONS

   The following actions are prohibited without prior written permission:

   (a) Copying or redistributing Proprietary Code in source or modified form;

   (b) Modifying, adapting, or creating derivative works of the Proprietary
   Code;

   (c) Reverse engineering, decompiling, or attempting to reconstruct the
   internal implementation of the Proprietary Code, except where such
   rights are explicitly granted by applicable law;

   (d) Removing or altering copyright or attribution notices;

   (e) Redistributing modified versions of the Software under the same or
   confusingly similar name;

   (f) Using the Proprietary Code itself (not general ideas or concepts) to
   create a competing library that directly reuses or derives from the
   Software’s internal implementation.

